#%RAML 1.0 Trait
displayName: Correlatable
description: |
  Optional end-to-end tracing header. When the caller supplies a valid
  `X-Correlation-Id` (RFC 4122 v4 UUID) it is propagated to every downstream
  hop and echoed back on the response. When the header is omitted, the API
  generates a fresh UUID at the entry flow and returns it in the response
  header so the caller can pick it up.

  Malformed values (present but not a v4 UUID) are rejected with `400` via
  the standard error envelope declared by the `hasErrors` trait.
headers:
  X-Correlation-Id:
    displayName: Correlation ID
    description: |
      RFC 4122 v4 UUID identifying the request across every downstream hop.
      Echoed back on the response and included in every log line. If omitted,
      the API generates one and returns it.
    type: string
    pattern: '^[0-9a-fA-F]{8}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{4}-[0-9a-fA-F]{12}$'
    required: false
    example: 5f9c2e1a-3b8d-4f7e-9a1c-2d4e6f8a0b3c
